WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:06.432
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and they did
some very big comic book moments on Walking

00:00:06.432 --> 00:00:09.520
Dead this week so we need to talk about those
and the big WTF cliffhanger at the end.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.469
Quick Reminder new giveaway starts now.

00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:15.039
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment.

00:00:15.039 --> 00:00:17.010
Lots of stuff to get through, so let’s get
right in it.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.380
Careful for spoilers from episode 2 if you
haven’t seen it yet.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.140
Starting with Top 5 moments.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.759
Number 5 - Everyone Recaps the back half of
season 4 for each other

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:29.060
There were a lot of interactions we’d been
waiting for like Rick confronting Tara.

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:31.350
Which totally didn’t go down the way I expected.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:34.540
He totally gave her a pass.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:43.700
I mean, she’s a cast regular.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:53.540
So she’s not going anywhere, but up till
she confessed her sins to Maggie in the church,

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:56.980
Tara stil felt like she was on everyone’s
shit list.

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:59.780
I’m really glad they’re able to act like
a family.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.660
Who is apparently led by Baby Judith.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:07.140
I loved the joke about Judith calling Rick
on the decision to go to DC.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:11.789
I mean he made the decision but it’s all
about staying together.

00:01:11.789 --> 00:01:18.020
Daryl couldn’t get Carol to fess up about
what she’d been through a la Lizze and Mika

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:20.420
but she did crack a smile.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:25.130
And yes, I totally think she was about to
bail on them when Daryl found her.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:27.670
Not bail per se, but just leave them.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:30.960
As if she didn’t feel like she fit in with
the group anymore.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.969
I’ve heard that the Carol Daryl story will
diverge, like that moment they took off in

00:01:33.969 --> 00:01:36.510
the car was the beginning of a new story arc
for them.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:42.149
I don’t know if they’ll find Beth, but
they might be how the show takes us back to

00:01:42.149 --> 00:01:44.119
Atlanta.

00:01:44.119 --> 00:01:47.250
The hospital where Beth is at is a big location,
I think that’s near Atlanta somewhere.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.850
And supposedly we’ll get a Beth scene in
episode 3.

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:52.189
So we’ll find out what’s up.

00:01:52.189 --> 00:01:54.030
Number 4 - Meet Father Gabriel

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:58.439
I’ve talked about him in a few of my bonus
videos before but as you could see, he holed

00:01:58.439 --> 00:02:01.740
himself up in his church for months after
the apocalpyse started.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.399
Based on the scratches on the outside “You’ll
Burn For This.”

00:02:04.399 --> 00:02:09.910
It sounds like the show is staying faithful
to the comics.

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:17.430
I feel like it was pretty obvious what he
did based on Detective Carl’s work and Gabriel’s

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:21.349
reaction to the walkers, but I’ll put this
spoiler tag up while I talk about him in the

00:02:21.349 --> 00:02:24.129
comics….okay..

00:02:24.129 --> 00:02:27.540
So in the comics, Gabriel just refused to
let people inside the church.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:32.150
He locked himself inside for months and survived
off the canned food drive they had done.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:36.890
During the apocalypse most people would probably
go to churches and hospitals for shelter and

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:37.890
supplies.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.800
so naturally he turned all those people away.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:40.879
And he knew all of them.

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:41.879
He was their minister.

00:02:41.879 --> 00:02:44.020
So he’s living with the guilt of that.”

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:45.200
okay, comics talk over.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:50.170
Like Carl said, something crazy went down,
but he’s not the villain.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:54.390
The church though, from the looks of the final
scene and the episode 3 teaser, will be a

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:56.790
battleground between the survivors and the
Termites.

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:57.790
Or The Hunters.

00:02:57.790 --> 00:02:59.510
I guess technically we can call them that
now.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:04.069
It’s possible they could wrap up the Church
storyline in the next episode and move on

00:03:04.069 --> 00:03:05.069
to DC.

00:03:05.069 --> 00:03:06.579
The Hunters storyline in the comics isn’t
super long.

00:03:06.579 --> 00:03:11.030
But Gareth is a series regular, so there is
some confusion as to what they’ll do with

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:14.719
that character.

00:03:14.719 --> 00:03:17.439
Number 3 - The Food Bank

00:03:17.439 --> 00:03:24.209
This was the big action set piece like the
store at the beginning of season 4.

00:03:24.209 --> 00:03:26.910
Remember that’s where we lost Beth’s most
recent boyfriend.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:29.930
So of course it fits that something terrible
would happen to someone in a very similar

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:30.930
scene.

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:34.829
Actually I think it was bob that got trapped
that time too.

00:03:34.829 --> 00:03:39.579
If I were superstitious I could say Bob has
been living on borrowed time since that rooftop

00:03:39.579 --> 00:03:40.579
collapse.

00:03:40.579 --> 00:03:41.860
Plus there was the time that the Walker only
bit “his bandage”.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:45.800
Every season they always try to top themselves
with a big epic walker scene like this.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:49.930
I still feel like the season 4 scene was crazier
in terms of tension.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:53.739
But that might be because spending all this
time making walking dead videos has desensitized

00:03:53.739 --> 00:03:54.739
me.

00:03:54.739 --> 00:03:58.799
And I just can’t tell what’s scary anymore.

00:03:58.799 --> 00:04:02.140
Gabriel is a total weakling but I did feel
sympathy for him.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:05.879
That area is a really small town, so of course
he would know everyone at the food bank.

00:04:05.879 --> 00:04:07.769
He’d seen all of them just a few months
ago.

00:04:07.769 --> 00:04:12.620
And when he made like Jesus on the cross here,
that walker coming for him looked like one

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:16.950
of his aldermen or whatever you call the people
that work really closely with preachers.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:19.180
He had been extra close to her.

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:22.870
So it would be like a best friend coming for
you.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:25.319
Number 2 - The Washington DC Pitch

00:04:25.319 --> 00:04:27.500
Abraham sells everyone, they’re going.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:33.600
Right after they deal with Gareth and his
Hunters.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:40.330
Eugene for all his mullet fast talking did
make a lot of sense.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:44.580
DC is a major city with all the supplies and
shelter they need to last indefinitely.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:50.009
So even if the cure took 20 years to fix things,
they could wait it out there.

00:04:50.009 --> 00:04:56.090
Please comic book readers, use spoiler tags
when talking about Eugene and the cure.

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:59.199
The toast scene had this really nice calming
effect on me.

00:04:59.199 --> 00:05:05.349
Most of the time you’re in oh shit mode
reaching for Katana’s that aren’t there.

00:05:05.349 --> 00:05:10.500
I’m interested to see how the church bus
in the trailer here, ends up being used for

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:12.750
a Dukes of Hazzard moment.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:13.750
Walking Dead Dukes of Hazzard.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:16.690
That was the bus that Gabriel said they could
take.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:19.840
So this scene could be from next week or it
could have something to do with the battle

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:23.849
with Gareth.

00:05:23.849 --> 00:05:27.780
And my Number 1 WTF Moment - Bob Stokey and
The Hunters

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:32.620
For anyone that had questions, Bob went out
into the woods to die.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:38.380
He had been bitten and just not told anyone.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:41.970
during the food bank swimming pool fight.

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:44.889
Interesting that he still had sex with Sasha.

00:05:44.889 --> 00:05:47.780
She’s going to be pissed about a lot of
things next week.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.780
Gareth and the Hunters captured him without
knowing he’d been bitten.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:52.949
And yes, they cut part of his leg off and
ate it while he was passed out.

00:05:52.949 --> 00:05:54.660
This is a scene right out of the comic.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:58.110
They left it on a cliffhanger, so I won’t
go too deep into what happens next.

00:05:58.110 --> 00:05:59.990
But if you want to read more about it.

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:04.300
Just read the Tainted meat part of Volume
11 of the comic before next week.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.199
It’s going to get crazy.

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:10.660
And I know they had that whole scene about
Michonne not missing her Katana, but she’s

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:13.009
holding it right here in the trailer.

00:06:13.009 --> 00:06:19.270
So I’m guessing one of Gareth’s men has
it on him and that’s how she gets it back.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:23.639
Let me know though, what was your favorite
moment and let me know if you think Daryl

00:06:23.639 --> 00:06:25.560
and Carol will find out where beth is?

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:29.020
If you’ve read the comic you probably know
exactly what’s going to happen with the

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:33.680
people at the church, so I don’t want to
post too many spoilers about how that goes

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:34.680
down.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:38.289
Overall I gave the episode a B plus, I loved
the way they cut the early montage scenes

00:06:38.289 --> 00:06:39.849
with them traveling down the round.

00:06:39.849 --> 00:06:42.650
Bouncing back and forth between people talking.

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:47.610
If you want to rewatch an amazing intro scene.

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:51.310
Bob Stookey’s is probably the best.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.810
It has this amazing soundtrack.

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:58.570
It was during the back half of Season 4 but
I can’t remember which episode exactly it

00:06:58.570 --> 00:06:59.570
was in.

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:02.310
All those episodes are on Netflix right now,
so it’s super easy to re-watch them all.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:04.139
Even though they did a lot of comic book things
that telegraphed what the plot was going to

00:07:04.139 --> 00:07:07.530
be, I still felt like they were able to use
the father gabriel church mystery to create

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:08.530
some tension.

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:12.500
The episode was mostly an intro to his character.

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:18.229
The Hunters part was really just the last
couple of minutes.

00:07:18.229 --> 00:07:21.699
This is still the part of the season where
they set up the major story arcs, like the

00:07:21.699 --> 00:07:22.699
search for Beth.

00:07:22.699 --> 00:07:27.919
So don’t be surprised if episode 3 sets
up another big arc.

00:07:27.919 --> 00:07:34.260
Carl had a great performance, he’s like
the moral conscience of the group right now.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:36.229
Normally that would make me worried.

00:07:36.229 --> 00:07:42.610
But since he’s not a big powerful figure
I think he’s mostly safe.

00:07:42.610 --> 00:07:47.710
Scott Gimple and Kirkman said that they killed
TV Dale off early on because they felt like

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:53.420
offered a certain amount of comfort and safety
to the survivors and as writers, they wanted

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:55.220
to take that feeling of safety away.

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:58.230
Then the same thing happened to Herschel at
the prison.

00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:03.620
So you really need to get worried when a figure
of authority tells everyone that there’s

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:06.220
nothing to worry about and they can all rest
easy.

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:09.860
Rick is safe because he’s telling everyone
that they’re about to die.

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:11.380
There is no safety.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:22.449
In case you didn’t see it I posted a bonus
video explaining who the Hunters in the comics

00:08:22.449 --> 00:08:26.629
are and how they’re different from Gareth’s
hunters on the show.

00:08:26.629 --> 00:08:28.180
Click here to learn all about that.

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:29.590
And click here for my Q&amp;A video.

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:30.590
That will post tomorrow.

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:32.310
Thanks for watching, now let’s all high
five and eat some tainted meat.

